# G1.6j: the wired PCI and USB network cards and the PHYs they use, as
# modules (corerouter-init loads what the machine has; PHYs through the
# kernel's own request_module and /sbin/modprobe). The drivers the image
# builds in stay in linux.fragment, and this file's list comes from the
# kernel itself: every tristate under drivers/net/{ethernet,usb,phy,mdio,pcs},
# built once, keeping what has a pci:, usb:, auxiliary: or mdio: alias and
# what those need (docs/os-image.md tells how to refresh it for a new kernel).
#
# Left out on purpose: switch ASICs and SmartNICs with big firmware
# (Netronome, LiquidIO, Octeon EP, Mellanox Spectrum, Prestera), Wi-Fi, LTE
# and tethering (HSO, Sierra, QMI, MBIM, Huawei NCM, VL600, Kalmia, iPhone),
# PCMCIA cards.
#
# DWMAC_INTEL (Intel mGbE on Atom and Core boards) needs the clock framework,
# and the Atheros AR803x PHY the regulator one.
CONFIG_COMMON_CLK=y
CONFIG_REGULATOR=y
CONFIG_8139CP=m
CONFIG_ACENIC=m
CONFIG_ADAPTEC_STARFIRE=m
CONFIG_ADIN1100_PHY=m
CONFIG_ADIN_PHY=m
CONFIG_AIR_EN8811H_PHY=m
CONFIG_ALX=m
CONFIG_AMD8111_ETH=m
CONFIG_AMD_PHY=m
CONFIG_AMD_XGBE=m
CONFIG_AQTION=m
